The Golden Sparrows are an [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oreskian]] movement against the government, made up largely of people who served in the Oreskian military and who carry over the intelligence service's way of writing messages. They break into [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]] offices and other government buildings for what they need, and to keep their own refuges from being found.

They pass word in plain sight: coded notices printed in newspaper circulars, and marks left on doorposts and stoops that only members can read. Their safe houses are marked with a stone on the window sill, and their watchers check on those houses and use a set of recognised knocks. [[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]] and [[People/Althane/Lev|Lev]] belong to the movement, and Lev has done its killing; he murdered a writer who had written against the Sparrows, in a train station, with a pencil.

[[People/Althane/Masha|Masha]] leads them, and [[People/Althane/Wojciech|Wojciech]] carries her word through the city. They are strongest in the poor outskirts of [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/Sarengrad|Sarengrad]] and their headquarters is there. Only the [[Org/Althane/The First House|Oreskian government]] may run a medical facility, so the Sparrows keep mobile clinics in borrowed houses for those the government will not treat. Between them they have lost close to eight hundred people to the [[Phenomena/Althane/Wasting Fever|wasting fever]] in a year, and the First House found and closed one of their clinics, relocating everyone inside and denying their families any word of them.

They take an interest in the [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/Kerneyy Prison Outpost|Kerneyy Prison Outpost]], because many of the prisoners held there are their own.
